<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Abernethy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1807">1807</a>–<a href="/years/1877">1877</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Abernethy was a Methodist mission steward and merchant who was elected governor of the Provisional Government of Oregon in 1845, its only governor. He held office at Oregon City until 1849, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oregon-territory">Oregon Territory</a> was established, and oversaw the response to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cayuse-war">Cayuse War</a> after the Whitman killings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-abernethy.jpg" alt="George Abernethy" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Buchtel and Stolte · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_Abernethy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
